WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.317 --> 00:00:10.661
In this lesson, you will file your daily stand-up, and you will see your work in three different ways: on the board, in a list, and on a calendar.

2
00:00:11.513 --> 00:00:25.265
Every working day, spend two minutes on the daily update. It keeps your streak alive, and it means your manager never has to chase you. Click Daily update in the menu.

3
00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:39.686
First, tell the team what you finished today. Short and specific is best. For example, twenty calls, two school visits, and the invoice for Sunrise School.

4
00:00:40.542 --> 00:00:47.094
Second, say what is still pending. This is what you will pick up tomorrow.

5
00:00:47.955 --> 00:00:56.259
Third, mention any obstacles. Founders read these, and it is the fastest way to get help.

6
00:00:57.121 --> 00:01:04.441
Click the save button. You can edit your update as often as you like until midnight.

7
00:01:05.305 --> 00:01:14.617
Now let us look at your work. Click Board. Each task is a card, and the columns are the statuses.

8
00:01:15.478 --> 00:01:29.590
Drag a card to another column to change its status. Drop it in Done when you finish it. Use the filters at the top to narrow the board by person, department or priority.

9
00:01:30.449 --> 00:01:39.689
Next, click List. This is the same work as a sortable table. It is the best view for searching.

10
00:01:40.563 --> 00:01:48.867
Click a column heading, such as Due, to sort. Choose a priority and click Apply to filter.

11
00:01:49.756 --> 00:02:01.828
Finally, click Calendar to see every deadline laid out by date. Use the arrows to move between months. Overdue tasks are shown in red.

12
00:02:02.706 --> 00:02:13.890
KalamDesk also tells you when something needs you. Click the bell to see your notifications: new tasks, comments, reminders and kudos.

13
00:02:14.771 --> 00:02:27.851
You now know the daily routine: check My Day, work your tasks, and file your stand-up. In the next lesson, we cover leave, school visits, leads and expenses.
